# @safe-global/safe-contracts@1.4.1 declares a peer dependency on the
# ethers v5 line (ethers@5.4.0), but this project only ever consumes its
# compiled Solidity artifacts (deploySafe.js, test/SafeOwnership.test.js) —
# never its JS SDK, which is the only part that actually needs ethers v5 at
# runtime. Meanwhile hardhat-ethers v4 (the toolchain this project's own
# scripts/tests use) requires ethers v6. A plain `npm ci`/`npm install`
# with npm 7+'s default strict peer resolution hard-fails on this
# unsatisfiable-on-paper conflict (ERESOLVE) even though nothing in this
# repo ever exercises the code path that would actually need it resolved.
# Reproduced with a fresh `npm ci` outside Docker/CI too — this is a real,
# pre-existing gap, not an artifact of any particular build environment.
legacy-peer-deps=true
